@@ -1725,8 +1725,23 @@ fastify.mkcol('/', (req, reply) => {
 })
 ```
 
+`addHttpMethod` can also redefine the body support of a method that is already
+supported, including the standard ones. Since this changes how every route
+registered for that method is handled, Fastify emits the
+[`FSTWRN005`](./Warnings.md#FSTWRN005) warning unless the `override` option
+is set to `true`:
+
+```js
+// Emits FSTWRN005: GET is supported without a body by default
+fastify.addHttpMethod('GET', { hasBody: true })
+
+// Intentional override, no warning
+fastify.addHttpMethod('GET', { hasBody: true, override: true })
+```
+
 > ⚠ Warning:
-> `addHttpMethod` overrides existing methods.
+> Overriding a standard HTTP method may break the expectations of clients,
+> proxies and plugins. Prefer adding a non standard method instead.
 
